From 4d584f52ad46fd5648e7ab494a74430d24c54dee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:39:50 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add stealth transport (obfuscated, encrypted TCP)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

stealth runs the existing TCP engine — control channel, connection pool,
port forwarding, sniffer — unchanged, and wraps every tunnel connection in
an encrypted, obfuscated layer so DPI has nothing to fingerprint.

Construction (standard library only, no new dependency):
  - ephemeral X25519 per connection, mixed with the tunnel token via HKDF
    (forward secrecy; keys match only if both ends hold the token);
  - AES-256-GCM record layer, records padded inside the encryption;
  - responder sends an AES-GCM confirmation the initiator verifies, so a
    wrong token fails fast rather than hanging;
  - token-keyed AES-CTR obfuscation masks the length prefixes and the
    handshake and pads it, so the opening is uniform-random, varies every
    connection, and carries no fixed fingerprint.

A wrong-token peer cannot derive the keys: its records fail to
authenticate and the connection is dropped with nothing sent back.

Enable with transport = "stealth" and the same token on both ends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
